# Implementation Plan: LoRa V2 Hardware Upgrade & Robust Wiring Map

This plan details the migration of the Smart Waste Management LoRa firmware to **Version 2**. It addresses crucial power management, collision avoidance, regional frequency, security, and hardware boot stability issues. It also integrates the **SW-420 Vibration Sensor** to handle transient readings, animal/vandalism interference, and sanitation emptying alerts.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Boot Pin Safety Constraints:** ESP8266 has strict boot pin states:
> * `GPIO15 (D8)` must be **LOW** during boot.
> * `GPIO0 (D3)` and `GPIO2 (D4)` must be **HIGH** during boot.
> * We have carefully mapped the pins below so that default sensor behaviors (like HC-SR04 Echo pulling LOW) align with these boot requirements to prevent boot-loops.
>
> **Deep Sleep Hardware Link:**
> * For the transmitter to wake up from deep sleep, a physical wire **MUST** connect **D0 (GPIO16)** to the NodeMCU's **RST** pin.
> * The LoRa module's `RST` pin will be tied directly to the NodeMCU's **RST** pin line. This ensures the LoRa module resets automatically whenever the NodeMCU boots up or wakes from deep sleep, without wasting an extra GPIO.

